                <pb facs="0885" n="771" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg771"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">738.3915/421: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-05-28T20:00:00-05:00">May 28, 1931—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 29—12:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>[45.] The President has informed the Commandant of the Garde of the receipt of a
                    very strong note from the Dominican Government demanding the immediate
                    withdrawal of Haitian Garde patrols from the southern frontier region between
                    Fonds-Verrettes and Bananodu [<hi rendition="#italic">Banane?</hi>] and stating
                    that orders have been given to the Dominican army to clear the region of foreign
                    troops. A small force of Gardes has patrolled the border recently because of
                    constant complaints that Dominican forces were crossing the frontier and
                    mistreating Haitians on this side of the lines. While the extent which each
                    government should occupy in this region is a matter primarily for discussion
                    between them it is extremely important that the Dominican Government should not
                    attempt any attack on the Garde which would necessarily involve us. I urgently
                    recommend that the Dominican Government be warned to avoid any such action.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Santo Domingo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Munro</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
